  "summary_text": "Beacon onboarding\nOnboarding completion 58% → 73% in usability tests\nMobile layout and pricing page and color tokens\nMobile layout and next steps seen as one underlying problem\nNo clear owner for mobile layout\nPricing page is still pretty rough\nReal issue may be process rather than color tokens\nPreference to get more data rather than cut the scope\nNext steps and prototype and doc\nNext steps is kind of stuck\nPrototype is mostly cosmetic\nFeedback on prototype from the data folks: they had some good ideas\nReal issue may be avatar treatment rather than doc\nPreference to sanity check the assumptions rather than draw it on a whiteboard\nAction items and spacing and backlog\nAction items is not a big deal\nSpacing is kind of fragile honestly\nReal issue may be design critique rather than backlog\nNo clear owner for backlog\nPreference to map out the edge cases rather than draw it on a whiteboard\nMotion specs and component library and scope\nMotion specs and spreadsheet seen as one underlying problem\nComponent library is lower priority than we think\nComponent library is in good shape\nScope is weirdly controversial\nPreference to pair on it rather than timebox it\nTradeoffs and dark mode pass and spreadsheet\nTradeoffs is the easy part\nTradeoffs is a bit messy\nFeedback on dark mode pass from a few managers: they were pretty chill about it\nSpreadsheet is ahead of where i expected\nPreference to do it properly rather than run it by support",
  "summary_markdown": "### Beacon onboarding\n- Onboarding completion 58% → 73% in usability tests\n\n### Mobile layout and pricing page and color tokens\n- Mobile layout and next steps seen as one underlying problem\n  - No clear owner for mobile layout\n- Pricing page is still pretty rough\n- Real issue may be process rather than color tokens\n- Preference to get more data rather than cut the scope\n\n### Next steps and prototype and doc\n- Next steps is kind of stuck\n- Prototype is mostly cosmetic\n  - Feedback on prototype from the data folks: they had some good ideas\n- Real issue may be avatar treatment rather than doc\n- Preference to sanity check the assumptions rather than draw it on a whiteboard\n\n### Action items and spacing and backlog\n- Action items is not a big deal\n- Spacing is kind of fragile honestly\n- Real issue may be design critique rather than backlog\n  - No clear owner for backlog\n- Preference to map out the edge cases rather than draw it on a whiteboard\n\n### Motion specs and component library and scope\n- Motion specs and spreadsheet seen as one underlying problem\n- Component library is lower priority than we think\n  - Component library is in good shape\n- Scope is weirdly controversial\n- Preference to pair on it rather than timebox it\n\n### Tradeoffs and dark mode pass and spreadsheet\n- Tradeoffs is the easy part\n  - Tradeoffs is a bit messy\n- Feedback on dark mode pass from a few managers: they were pretty chill about it\n- Spreadsheet is ahead of where i expected\n- Preference to do it properly rather than run it by support",
  "private_notes_text": null,
  "private_notes_markdown": null,
